<title>UK: GECC sets 300 million mark five-year bond.</title>
<headline>GECC sets 300 million mark five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue was announced by lead manager Paribas Capital Markets.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GENERAL ELECTRIC CAPITAL CORP</p>
<p> AMT    300 MLN DEM   COUPON     4.875     MATURITY    06.FEB.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.59    PAY DATE    06.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    99.84     SPREAD	+30 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.75	PRAECIP     =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOV BOND  120 B0BL</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF AN MTN PROGRAMME</p>
